<title>UK: Crashed Saudi 747 hull insured for $36mln -sources.</title>
<headline>Crashed Saudi 747 hull insured for $36mln -sources.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hull of the Saudi Airlines Boeing 747 which crashed near New Delhi on Tuesday was insured for $36 million, according to insurance market sources.</p>
<p>Cover for the airliner, which collided with a Kazakhstan airliner in mid-air at around 1330 GMT, had been placed by a consortium of insurance brokers CT Bowring and Willis Corroon.</p>
<p>The lead insurer was the Aerial syndicate at Lloyd's of London, and market sources said the bulk of the claim for the airliner' hull was likely to land on the London insurance market.</p>
</text>
